## Summary
- make Swagger security definitions environment-aware;
- in Development, expose `X-Tenant-Id` and `X-Dev-User` and require both for Swagger requests;
- in non-Development environments, expose only the Bearer JWT scheme;
- keep the existing Swashbuckle 10 API configuration and Swagger UI route unchanged.

## Root cause
The Development authentication handler requires `X-Tenant-Id` and `X-Dev-User`, but Swagger's global security requirement referenced only `Bearer`. Swagger UI could load, while local "Try it out" calls were sent without the required development headers.

## Validation
The change is isolated to `src/PersonalWealth.Api/Program.cs`. Main was green on the latest recorded CI run; this PR should be validated by the repository CI before merging.

