This PR hardens the RoomService TurboDB runtime ownership boundary after the Orm::C migration:

- adds `iris_orm_store_owner_close()` as an explicit retryable close operation;
- preserves the runtime strong reference when `orm_runtime_close()` returns BUSY instead of releasing it;
- keeps outbox/ledger teardown objects intact when the ORM runtime has not quiesced, so destroy can be retried;
- adds test-only TurboDb.Driver Plugin fixtures without libpq;
- covers wrong canonical driver id, connection failure without fallback, and BUSY close -> retry.

The fixture publishes the canonical Plugin ABI and only implements the minimal RAW SQL command surface needed for owner bootstrap. It is test-only and is not installed or linked into production packages.

Transaction rollback/data semantics remain tracked by #90 and are intentionally not mixed into this lifetime-focused PR.
